  "file": "src/server/workers.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A worker sends an invalid text byte inside an otherwise valid event or completion report. The coordinator acknowledges the report and saves replacement characters instead of rejecting the malformed input.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/limitless-730-adjudicate-head.ts\"",
    "output": "F2 events {\"http\":200,\"stored\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\ufffd\"}],\"state\":\"leased\"}\nF2 result {\"http\":200,\"state\":\"done\",\"storedFinalText\":\"\ufffd\"}\nBase decoder behavior {\"seq\":0,\"events\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\ufffd\"}]}"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary probe submitted raw 0xff inside JSON strings to HEAD's actual request handler and inspected a real temporary SQLite database. Bun.serve was intercepted to capture the handler because the sandbox refused a loopback listener; transport was not reproduced. HEAD decodes with `JSON.parse(Buffer.concat(chunks).toString(\"utf8\"))`, then validates and persists the substituted strings. Base used `await req.json()`; the control probe confirms that decoder also substituted invalid UTF-8. This existing permissive behavior is newly exposed through durable agent-event/result ingestion. The response commit uses `new TextDecoder(\"utf-8\", { fatal: true })` and adds rejection tests for both routes."
  },
